\section{Rewriting Artifact Control}
\label{app:artifact_control}

Same-style double-rewrite (DR) controls quantify the rewriting artifact: the proportion of pairs where the judge prefers the original over its same-style DR.
Both judges systematically prefer LLM-polished text across axes (Table~\ref{tab:artifact}).
For verbosity, the near-zero original win rate indicates that rewriting quality dominates when content is held constant, validating the GEE decomposition that separates style from artifact effects.

